I take care of my pets and never have problems with them getting angry. 
Exercise usual care and I don't think you will find that a major 
trouble. Non-domestic pets usually don't have to be fed, which is a plus 
most of the time, but this can also be a hindrance when you want to 
increase their tameness.

If you want to do some more pet switching, my preferred pets are:
1. Archon (standard "best pet" candidate, though I'm not sure you can 
get one from a polymorph trap)
2. Iron Golem (has a special weakness though, and you will need a magic 
whistle to stand its slow movement)
3. Purple Worm (for this also you will need a magic whistle to stand its 
slow movement)
These pets can all attain quite high levels, which means they will help 
you out through the whole game, not being afraid to attack high level 
enemies. And they are absolute killers for almost anything in your way.
Dragons are nice too, but not as nice as those above IMHO, and note that 
tame dragons never use their breath weapon.

Besides a magic whistle, a stethoscope is also nice to have to check 
your pet's status. Some people use leashes, I seldom find a need for 
these devices. Use wands of speed monster to bring up the speed of your 
pets.

An annoying thing might be that you have to protect priests, shopkeepers 
and other dungeon dwellers that you want to keep alive. Lock away your 
power-pet before doing friendly business.

